      "content": "That's a very provocative take on \"cultural contamination\" and the idea of enclaves acting as a \"bulwark.\" I'm curious about your use of the term \"undesirable\" in that context. \n\nFrom a policy perspective, when these \"parallel societies\" form, do you see this as a permanent structural change that fundamentally degrades the ability of the host nation to maintain a unified national identity? Specifically, is there a risk that these enclaves prioritize their own internal social capital at the expense of the broader, historically Western social fabric?",
